1
00:00:03,051 --> 00:00:04,663
Red, orange, yellow…

2
00:00:04,713 --> 00:00:08,484
In autumn, the leaves change color, then fall.

3
00:00:08,534 --> 00:00:10,777
But where did the green go?

4
00:00:11,552 --> 00:00:13,392
Noah compares a green summer

5
00:00:13,442 --> 00:00:15,416
leaf and a yellow autumn leaf.

6
00:00:15,466 --> 00:00:16,900
Same tree, same shape…

7
00:00:16,950 --> 00:00:18,435
but the green is gone!

8
00:00:19,232 --> 00:00:20,746
Discovery mission!

9
00:00:23,275 --> 00:00:23,879
Mini mode!

10
00:00:23,929 --> 00:00:27,151
The leaf is full of a green coloring, chlorophyll,

11
00:00:27,201 --> 00:00:29,769
which catches sunlight to feed the tree.

12
00:00:29,819 --> 00:00:32,502
And in summer, it hides the other colors.

13
00:00:33,290 --> 00:00:35,508
When the days get shorter and it gets cold,

14
00:00:35,558 --> 00:00:38,674
the tree stops making chlorophyll and takes back its pieces.

15
00:00:38,724 --> 00:00:39,676
So the green fades,

16
00:00:39,726 --> 00:00:42,522
and the yellow and orange hidden since summer appear!

17
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:43,997
And the red?

18
00:00:44,047 --> 00:00:44,992
That one is new:

19
00:00:45,042 --> 00:00:48,601
some trees make it just before letting go of their leaves.

20
00:00:48,651 --> 00:00:50,841
Then a layer of cells cuts the stem…

21
00:00:50,891 --> 00:00:52,073
and the leaf falls.

22
00:00:52,882 --> 00:00:54,219
But the tree doesn't die:

23
00:00:54,269 --> 00:00:57,715
it rests through winter and grows green leaves again in spring.

24
00:00:57,765 --> 00:00:59,708
Meanwhile, leaf piles are all ours!

25
00:01:00,480 --> 00:01:02,795
And that's why leaves change color.

26
00:01:04,039 --> 00:01:07,191
The green disappears and reveals the hidden yellow;

27
00:01:07,241 --> 00:01:09,438
the red, though, is made in autumn.

28
00:01:10,279 --> 00:01:10,956
With an adult:

29
00:01:11,006 --> 00:01:14,335
collect leaves and line them up from the greenest to the reddest.

30
00:01:14,385 --> 00:01:16,204
Which one still has a little green?

31
00:01:17,738 --> 00:01:19,963
And how do fish breathe underwater?

32
00:01:20,013 --> 00:01:21,312
The answer tomorrow.
